{"kind":"stack","id":"s1","title":"How sounds are made","theme":{"background":"#F4F9FF","foreground":"#1B2A41","font":"Trebuchet MS, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Vibration"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Vibration is a quick back-and-forth shaking movement. Vibrations make sound."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1-next","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1n-t","content":"Sound"},{"type":"text","id":"c1n-e","content":"Sound is a signal that travels through the air and reaches our ears."}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"image","id":"c2-img","picto":"bell"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-q","content":"What is making the sound when a bell rings?"},{"type":"button","id":"c2-a","label":"The bell is vibrating","why":"A vibrating object pushes the air and makes sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"The bell is getting heavier","why":"Pupils may think weight changes the sound, not the shaking.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c2-c","label":"The bell is getting colder","why":"Pupils may link temperature to sound, when it is the vibration that matters.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"When you pluck a guitar string, what happens to the string?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"It vibrates","why":"Plucking makes the string move back and forth quickly.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"It stays perfectly still","why":"Pupils may think the sound comes from the guitar body alone.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"It turns into water","why":"A silly mix-up that a pupil would not really make, so replace this option.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"You find a drum. Do you tap it gently or hit it hard?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Tap it gently","why":"A gentle tap makes small, quiet vibrations.","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4a"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Hit it hard","why":"A hard hit makes big, loud vibrations.","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4b"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4a","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4a-t","content":"The drum gives a soft, quiet sound. Its skin moves only a little."},{"type":"button","id":"c4a-btn","label":"Continue","why":"Moves on to the next question.","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4b","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4b-t","content":"The drum gives a loud, booming sound. Its skin shakes hard and fast."},{"type":"button","id":"c4b-btn","label":"Continue","why":"Moves on to the next question.","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"Which of these makes a sound by vibrating?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"A ruler twanged over a table edge","why":"Twanging makes the ruler vibrate, and the vibration makes the sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"A still, empty cup","why":"A still object makes no vibration, so no sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-c","label":"A closed book on a shelf","why":"A closed, resting book is not shaking, so it makes no sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-q","content":"How do you feel your throat make a sound when you hum?"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-a","label":"Your vocal cords vibrate","why":"Your vocal cords shake quickly, making the sound you hear.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Your throat gets hotter","why":"Pupils may think heat makes the sound, not the vibration.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c6-c","label":"Your teeth stop moving","why":"Pupils may confuse the teeth with the part that makes the sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"What must a sound travel through to reach your ears?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"Air","why":"Sound travels through air to reach your ears.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Sand only","why":"Pupils may think sound needs solid things, not air.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"Empty space with nothing in it","why":"Sound cannot travel where there is nothing to carry it.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"A tuning fork is struck and then touched lightly to water. What do you see?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"The water ripples","why":"The vibrating fork makes the water move, showing vibration.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"The water freezes","why":"Pupils may think sound makes things cold, which it does not.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"The water turns green","why":"A silly change that does not come from vibration, so replace this option.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"Which of these makes the loudest sound?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"A drum hit hard","why":"Harder hits make bigger vibrations and louder sounds.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"A drum tapped gently","why":"Gentle taps make small vibrations and quiet sounds.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"A drum held still","why":"A still drum makes no vibration, so no sound.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-h","content":"You finished: how sounds are made"},{"type":"text","id":"c10-m","content":"Great work! Remember: vibrations make sound, and sound travels through air to your ears."}],"actions":[]}}
